{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T13:32:48.148Z","data":{"text":"Task 3 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented deterministic OpenSpec delta merging.\n\n**Created `src/core/delta.ts`** — a pure engine:\n- `parseDelta` extracts `ADDED`/`MODIFIED`/`REMOVED` requirement blocks and `RENAMED` FROM/TO pairs\n- `parseRequirement`/`parseScenario` extract requirement names, bodies, scenario names, and `**WHEN**`/`**THEN**` bullets\n- `mergeDelta` executes strictly `RENAMED -> REMOVED -> MODIFIED -> ADDED`, creates a new capability spec from the delta `Purpose` when no base exists, and throws `DeltaMergeError` with a fixed message for missing targets\n- `parseCapabilitySpec`/`serializeCapabilitySpec` for canonical, byte-stable round-tripping\n\n**Updated `src/watcher/archiver.ts`**:\n- New `applyOpenSpecDeltas` merges each `<change>/specs/<capability>/spec.md` into `openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md`\n- `applyDelta` applies OpenSpec deltas first, then preserves the legacy prose-delta behavior; change-doc resolution now uses the proposal→spec fallback\n\n**Added `tests/delta-merge.test.ts`** — 11 tests covering all six acceptance lines (including the inline golden-file byte-for-byte rebuild) plus archiver create/update and no-op cases.\n\nVerification: target test passes (11/11); full suite 367/367; `tsc --noEmit` and `biome check` clean. Result written to `specs/016-openspec-artifacts/.run/results/3.md`.\n\nNotable deviation documented: `paths.openspecRoot` is read defensively with an `'openspec'` fallback because task 1's config change is not in the working tree; once it lands, the accessor picks it up without further changes."}}
